	(label "BOUT2" (at 190.5 124.46 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6c6be982-012c-5ca9-a6d3-9265fb5447c0"))
	(text "NOTES - Rev B: power rerouted so the Nano stays in spec and motor current bypasses it\n1. POWER: A1 runs from its own USB-C port (5 V, 500 mA max) through pigtail J2, which plugs in rather than wiring to an A1 pin.\n    VIN (rated 6-21 V) and the 5V pin stay unused. Unplug J2 before connecting a computer to program A1.\n2. MOTOR VOLTAGE: 3 V motors see about 5 V, slightly more than Rev A. The firmware drives AIN/BIN at 100% (digitalWrite, no PWM).\n3. ASEN/BSEN: grounded per the TI datasheet. Wire them only if the breakout brings them out and has no sense resistors of its own.\n    FAULT is unused. U1 pin numbers are arbitrary because header order varies between breakouts.\n4. A0 must stay unconnected: the firmware seeds random() from its floating input with analogRead(A0).\n5. J1 shows only VBUS and GND. For C-to-C adapters to supply 5 V, the breakout needs 5.1k pull-downs on CC1 and CC2.\n6. M1, M2, SW1, SW2 and the J2 pigtail are off-board parts, wired by hand, with no footprints assigned." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 138.43 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "68181c83-d70b-598d-bb9f-d6c97651a66e"))
	(text "USB-C POWER INPUT" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 58.42 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c87847b5-1704-5d70-8cf3-648fb2945b33"))
	(text "CONTROLLER" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 76.2 58.42 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6ba2328b-c4b9-5a5d-a6da-55d0ec9d662f"))
	(text "MOTOR DRIVER" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 144.78 58.42 0) (effects (font (size 2.0 2.0)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bf8ab5f4-24ba-55ce-acea-659ffd9d6f3e"))
